Sval: put the Picture-in-Picture toggle in the video's top corner

The toggle sat at 70% of the video's height less 40px, on its right edge,
which reads as a control floating at no particular place on the video.
It sits in the corner instead, as far from the top as from the side
(--pip-toggle-distanceFromVideoEdge). A site's own toggle policy
(PictureInPictureToggleChild's policy attribute) still places it.

Once the toggle is the compact icon (has-used), nothing on it says what it
does. Hovered or focused, it shows its label in a pill that grows from the
icon, the first-time card's label without its explainer.

diff --git a/toolkit/themes/shared/media/pipToggle.css b/toolkit/themes/shared/media/pipToggle.css
index bd09de68b9..e49f99ff22 100644
--- a/toolkit/themes/shared/media/pipToggle.css
+++ b/toolkit/themes/shared/media/pipToggle.css
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
   color: inherit;
   border: none;
   text-align: unset;
-  top: calc(70% - 40px);
+  top: var(--pip-toggle-distanceFromVideoEdge);
   opacity: 0;
   padding-inline: 0;
   transition: opacity 200ms;
@@ -397,3 +397,50 @@
 .pip-wrapper.experiment:not([policy="hidden"]):focus-visible > .pip-expanded {
   box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 96, 223, 0.9);
 }
+
+/* SVAL - PIP STYLING */
+
+/* The compact toggle is a round button, as Sval's own buttons are. Hovered
+ * or focused, it says what it does: a pill grows from it toward the video's
+ * middle and carries its label, and the toggle's icon (.pip-icon, the last
+ * child) stays on top at the pill's end. */
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"] {
+  --pip-border-radius-toggle: 999px;
+}
+
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"]:not([small-video]) > .pip-expanded {
+  display: flex;
+  height: var(--pip-icon-width-with-margins);
+  min-width: 0;
+  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
+  border-radius: 999px;
+  background-color: rgba(12, 12, 13, 0.9);
+  pointer-events: none;
+}
+
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"]:not([small-video]):is(.hovering, :focus-visible) > .pip-expanded {
+  opacity: 1;
+  scale: 1;
+  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
+  padding-bottom: 0;
+  pointer-events: auto;
+}
+
+/* The pill draws the background, so the round button's own one would show
+ * as a second shape inside it. */
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"]:not([small-video]):is(.hovering, :focus-visible) > .pip-small {
+  opacity: 0;
+}
+
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"] > .pip-icon {
+  z-index: 1;
+}
+
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"] > .pip-expanded > .pip-explainer,
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"] > .pip-expanded > .pip-icon-label > .pip-icon {
+  display: none;
+}
+
+.pip-wrapper[has-used][position="right"] > .pip-expanded > .pip-icon-label > .pip-label {
+  margin-inline: 16px calc(var(--pip-icon-width-with-margins) + 8px);
+}
